id: soar
name: Soar
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
soars: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Take to the air. Defense Value 1(bT) higher until your next turn begins, and go up or
  down a rank of High Environment - or into the Low Sky from the ground.
text: >
  Soar Maneuver [1/Round]: Soar through the skies like a bird!
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: Free
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Increase your Defense Value by 1(bT) until the start of your next turn.
  Additionally, if not in a High Environment, you can enter the Low Sky Environment. If
  in a High Environment, you can increase your rank of High Environment by +/- 1 Rank,
  where if it would become 0 then you enter the normal Battle Environment for the Square
  you are occupying.

---

# The Maneuver the High Environment rules have been pointing at since they arrived. It was
# held back twice: once because the ranks did not exist, and once because the table asked.
#
# --- The Defense Value ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Increase your Defense Value by 1(bT) until the start of your next turn."
#
# A duration, so it is a mark: `soaring`, whose file carries the bonus. Brace's shape, and
# Brace's edge - a start edge is never ahead of you during your own turn.
#
# Not the same thing as being in the air. "Additionally" is the entry's own word: the mark
# is one effect and the height is another, and a character may Soar and stay where they
# are. One is what you did this turn; the other is where you are standing.
#
# --- The height -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "If not in a High Environment, you can enter the Low Sky Environment. If in a High
# Environment, you can increase your rank of High Environment by +/- 1 Rank, where if it
# would become 0 then you enter the normal Battle Environment for the Square you are
# occupying."
#
# Which is one rule with two branches and no third: from the ground there is one place to
# go, and from the air there are two. `soars: true` is what asks - the question is the
# player's and the answer depends on where they already are, which is not a thing a script
# in this language can ask before it runs.
#
# "Can", both times, so the height is offered and not taken: the answer includes staying
# where you are, and the Defense Value is still bought with the Action.
#
# Rank 0 is the ground by the rules' own definition, so "if it would become 0 then you
# enter the normal Battle Environment" needs nothing of its own: dropping from the Low Sky
# sets the rank to 0, and the Battle Environment the character has been carrying all along
# is the one they land in. That field was deliberately left alone when they went up.
#
# --- Free for a Minion -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Minions: Free." There are no Minions in this system, which the Brace, Analysis and Hype
# files all say about their own Minion lines. Carried as printed and read by nobody, which
# is the library's convention - a header for it would be one more thing declared in one
# place and read in none.

[on used]
gain(soaring);
expires(soaring, start-of-next-turn);
